# mod/ conventions

- Patches are **minimally invasive**; document why each patch exists (`ADR-0004`).
- Prefer upstream contributions when practical; do not grow silent forks without need.
- When touching a patch, **check whether a newer Brightway (or related) dependency already provides the behavior** and remove or shrink the monkey-patch if so; note the check in the patch comment or nearby README.
- Keep patches compatible with upstream version ranges declared in `pyproject.toml` / conda recipe.
- Test thoroughly — these change third-party behavior at import time.
- Do not relocate unrelated AB features into `mod/`; this package is for third-party adaptation only.
